WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
Two households go shopping.

2
00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:06.300
Every price they pay includes
a 20 per cent sales tax.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.090
One household earns 20,000 a year.

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.730
The other earns 100,000.

5
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.810
At the till, the richer household
hands over far more tax:

6
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.210
8,333, against 3,000.

7
00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.720
So the richer household is hit harder.

8
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.810
Or is it?

9
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.000
Could a tax take a bigger bite
from the poorer household,

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.590
even while the richer one pays more?

11
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.740
In this mission, you'll sort
taxes into direct and indirect,

12
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.790
and work out average and
marginal tax rates from a set

13
00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.600
of income tax bands.

14
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.190
Then you'll compare three kinds of tax,

15
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.070
and see what a flat tax really does.

16
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.260
Your mission: find out how
to judge which households

17
00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.930
a tax hits hardest.
